(25, '{\"ar\":\"الصيدلية\",\"en\":\"Pharmacy\"}', NULL, NULL, '{\"ar\":\"22\",\"en\":\"Al nas hospital\"}', '{\"en\":\"Why Choose Al Nas Hospital for Burn, Plastic & Reconstructive Surgery\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"<p>The unit provides full-spectrum burn care, integrating medical, surgical, rehabilitative, and psychological support. Services extend from critical care management in the early stages to reconstructive surgery and long-term rehabilitation, ensuring patients receive interdisciplinary continuous care.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p>4566</p>\"}', NULL, '[{\"uuid\":\"0158c9e1-e84f-43e9-875b-25f272adff38\",\"title\":{\"en\":\"Clinical Programs\",\"ar\":\"ww\"},\"content\":{\"en\":\"Discover our clinical programs delivering expert, patient-centered care.\",\"ar\":null}},{\"uuid\":\"a0ee469c-9eb6-40cb-9f97-82c39d5cd454\",\"title\":{\"en\":\"Departments, Umbrellas of Excellence & Centers\",\"ar\":\"ee\"},\"content\":{\"en\":\"Explore our specialties offering comprehensive care across multiple fields.\",\"ar\":null}},{\"uuid\":\"58ae3b88-3111-4fc6-8506-ae71eb4338a8\",\"title\":{\"en\":\"Outcomes\",\"ar\":\"dd\"},\"content\":{\"en\":\"Learn how our care transforms patient outcomes and quality of life.\",\"ar\":null}}]', '{\"en\":\"Al nas hospital\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"<p>Ali isn’t just a child—he’s a story of hope.<br>Ali is a little hero, and his wound tells a story of hope that begins anew. Help us equip the Burn Unit at Al Nas Hospital so we can treat more children and ease their pain.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p>علي مش مجرد طفل، علي قصة أمل<br>علي بطل صغير، وجرحه حكاية أمل بتبدأ من جديد. ساعدنا نجهز قسم الحروق في مستشفى الناس علشان نعالج أطفال أكتر ونخفف ألمهم.</p>\"}', NULL, '{\"en\":\"al nas hospital\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\" Al Nas Hospital Clinical Programs\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"al nas hospital\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"Departments\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"<p>The unit provides full-spectrum burn care, integrating medical, surgical, rehabilitative, and psychological support. Services extend from critical care management in the early stages to reconstructive surgery and long-term rehabilitation, ensuring patients receive interdisciplinary continuous care.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '[{\"0\":{\"title\":\"out 1\",\"content\":\"<p>Our department is equipped with advanced imaging technologies including 3D echocardiography, CT, and MRI, ensuring precise diagnostics, safer interventions, and improved outcomes.<\\/p><p>With renowned professors and consultants who bring international expertise, we excel in treating complex and high-risk cases such as chronic total occlusions, high-risk percutaneous interventions, and adult congenital heart disease.<\\/p><p>Care is delivered through a collaborative heart team approach that integrates cardiologists, surgeons, and imaging specialists, supported by extensive case experience, innovative non-surgical options such as TAVI and TAVR, and a strong commitment to minimally invasive procedures for faster recovery.<\\/p><p>As a teaching hospital, we are dedicated to academic excellence through fellowships, international collaborations, and continuous training.<\\/p><p>Our patient-centered model ensures accessible, lifelong care including specialized adult congenital programs, while maintaining the highest standards of quality, safety, and evidence-based practice through ongoing audits and performance reviews.<\\/p>\",\"embed\":null},\"1\":{\"title\":\"out 2\",\"content\":\"<p>Our department is equipped with advanced imaging technologies including 3D echocardiography, CT, and MRI, ensuring precise diagnostics, safer interventions, and improved outcomes.<\\/p><p>With renowned professors and consultants who bring international expertise, we excel in treating complex and high-risk cases such as chronic total occlusions, high-risk percutaneous interventions, and adult congenital heart disease.<\\/p><p>Care is delivered through a collaborative heart team approach that integrates cardiologists, surgeons, and imaging specialists, supported by extensive case experience, innovative non-surgical options such as TAVI and TAVR, and a strong commitment to minimally invasive procedures for faster recovery.<\\/p><p>As a teaching hospital, we are dedicated to academic excellence through fellowships, international collaborations, and continuous training.<\\/p><p>Our patient-centered model ensures accessible, lifelong care including specialized adult congenital programs, while maintaining the highest standards of quality, safety, and evidence-based practice through ongoing audits and performance reviews.<\\/p>\",\"embed\":null},\"content\":{\"en\":\"<p>Discover the medical specialties at Al Nas Hospital, where expert teams provide care across<\\/p>\",\"ar\":\"<p><\\/p>\"},\"embeds\":[{\"embed\":\"embed\"}],\"title\":{\"en\":\"Outcomes\",\"ar\":null}}]', '2025-12-24 08:31:48', '2026-02-11 14:42:37', NULL, 0, 0, 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JoynCzHaY1g', '{\"ar\":null}', '{\"ar\":null}', '{\"ar\":null}', '{\"ar\":null}', NULL),
(26, '{\"ar\":\"الطب الطبيعي وإعادة التأهيل\",\"en\":\"Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation \"}', NULL, NULL, '{\"ar\":\"22\",\"en\":\"Al nas hospital\"}', '{\"en\":\"Why Choose Al Nas Hospital for Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation?\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"<p>At Al Nas Hospital’s Physiotherapy Department, we provide comprehensive, multidisciplinary care through close collaboration between physiotherapists, physicians, and surgeons, ensuring holistic management for every patient. Our state-of-the-art robotic and electrotherapy systems enhance rehabilitation outcomes, while specialized programs address the unique needs of critical care, pediatric, and sports medicine patients. Guided by evidence-based, internationally standardized rehabilitation pathways, our team focuses on restoring functional independence, facilitating return to work, and improving overall quality of life.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p>4566</p>\"}', NULL, '[{\"uuid\":\"0158c9e1-e84f-43e9-875b-25f272adff38\",\"title\":{\"en\":\"Clinical Programs\",\"ar\":\"ww\"},\"content\":{\"en\":\"Discover our clinical programs delivering expert, patient-centered care.\",\"ar\":null}},{\"uuid\":\"a0ee469c-9eb6-40cb-9f97-82c39d5cd454\",\"title\":{\"en\":\"Departments, Umbrellas of Excellence & Centers\",\"ar\":\"ee\"},\"content\":{\"en\":\"Explore our specialties offering comprehensive care across multiple fields.\",\"ar\":null}},{\"uuid\":\"58ae3b88-3111-4fc6-8506-ae71eb4338a8\",\"title\":{\"en\":\"Outcomes\",\"ar\":\"dd\"},\"content\":{\"en\":\"Learn how our care transforms patient outcomes and quality of life.\",\"ar\":null}}]', '{\"en\":\"Al nas hospital\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"Why Choose Al Nas Hospital for Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation?\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"<p>Al Nas Hospital’s Physiotherapy Department provides personalized rehabilitation for patients recovering from surgery, injuries, or critical illness. Our team works closely with doctors and surgeons to create tailored programs using advanced techniques like robotic therapy and electrotherapy. We follow evidence-based protocols to ensure safe and effective care, helping patients regain mobility, independence, and quality of life. Support and education are provided to patients and families throughout the recovery process.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, '{\"en\":\"al nas hospital\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\" Al Nas Hospital Clinical Programs\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"al nas hospital\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"Departments\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"<p>Our Physiotherapy Department offers specialized rehabilitation programs designed to support recovery, restore function, and improve quality of life across a range of medical and surgical conditions.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '[{\"0\":{\"title\":\"out 1\",\"content\":\"<p>Our department is equipped with advanced imaging technologies including 3D echocardiography, CT, and MRI, ensuring precise diagnostics, safer interventions, and improved outcomes.<\\/p><p>With renowned professors and consultants who bring international expertise, we excel in treating complex and high-risk cases such as chronic total occlusions, high-risk percutaneous interventions, and adult congenital heart disease.<\\/p><p>Care is delivered through a collaborative heart team approach that integrates cardiologists, surgeons, and imaging specialists, supported by extensive case experience, innovative non-surgical options such as TAVI and TAVR, and a strong commitment to minimally invasive procedures for faster recovery.<\\/p><p>As a teaching hospital, we are dedicated to academic excellence through fellowships, international collaborations, and continuous training.<\\/p><p>Our patient-centered model ensures accessible, lifelong care including specialized adult congenital programs, while maintaining the highest standards of quality, safety, and evidence-based practice through ongoing audits and performance reviews.<\\/p>\",\"embed\":null},\"1\":{\"title\":\"out 2\",\"content\":\"<p>Our department is equipped with advanced imaging technologies including 3D echocardiography, CT, and MRI, ensuring precise diagnostics, safer interventions, and improved outcomes.<\\/p><p>With renowned professors and consultants who bring international expertise, we excel in treating complex and high-risk cases such as chronic total occlusions, high-risk percutaneous interventions, and adult congenital heart disease.<\\/p><p>Care is delivered through a collaborative heart team approach that integrates cardiologists, surgeons, and imaging specialists, supported by extensive case experience, innovative non-surgical options such as TAVI and TAVR, and a strong commitment to minimally invasive procedures for faster recovery.<\\/p><p>As a teaching hospital, we are dedicated to academic excellence through fellowships, international collaborations, and continuous training.<\\/p><p>Our patient-centered model ensures accessible, lifelong care including specialized adult congenital programs, while maintaining the highest standards of quality, safety, and evidence-based practice through ongoing audits and performance reviews.<\\/p>\",\"embed\":null},\"content\":{\"en\":\"<p>Discover the medical specialties at Al Nas Hospital, where expert teams provide care across<\\/p>\",\"ar\":\"<p><\\/p>\"},\"embeds\":[{\"embed\":\"embed\"}],\"title\":{\"en\":\"Outcomes\",\"ar\":null}}]', '2025-12-24 08:31:48', '2026-02-10 13:14:31', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, '{\"ar\":null}', '{\"ar\":null}', '{\"ar\":null}', '{\"ar\":null}', NULL),
(27, '{\"ar\":\"التغذية العلاجية\",\"en\":\"Clinical Nutrition\"}', NULL, NULL, '{\"ar\":\"22\",\"en\":\"Al nas hospital\"}', '{\"en\":\"Why Choose Al Nas Hospital for Clinical Nutrition?\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"<p>At AL NAS Hospital’s Nutrition Department, we deliver specialized medical and surgical nutrition care tailored to each patient’s needs. Our team of clinical nutrition physicians and dietitians works hand in hand with cardiology, burns, diabetes, gastrointestinal, and transplant services to ensure nutrition is an integral part of every treatment plan. From personalized counseling to advanced enteral and parenteral feeding, we provide comprehensive support that promotes recovery, wound healing, and long-term wellness. Guided by international standards and a holistic, evidence-based approach, we place nutrition at the heart of patient care, while also extending our efforts to the community through awareness and education campaigns that encourage healthier lifestyles and disease prevention.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p>4566</p>\"}', NULL, '[{\"uuid\":\"0158c9e1-e84f-43e9-875b-25f272adff38\",\"title\":{\"en\":\"Clinical Programs\",\"ar\":\"ww\"},\"content\":{\"en\":\"Discover our clinical programs delivering expert, patient-centered care.\",\"ar\":null}},{\"uuid\":\"a0ee469c-9eb6-40cb-9f97-82c39d5cd454\",\"title\":{\"en\":\"Departments, Umbrellas of Excellence & Centers\",\"ar\":\"ee\"},\"content\":{\"en\":\"Explore our specialties offering comprehensive care across multiple fields.\",\"ar\":null}},{\"uuid\":\"58ae3b88-3111-4fc6-8506-ae71eb4338a8\",\"title\":{\"en\":\"Outcomes\",\"ar\":\"dd\"},\"content\":{\"en\":\"Learn how our care transforms patient outcomes and quality of life.\",\"ar\":null}}]', '{\"en\":\"Al nas hospital\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"<p>At Al Nas Hospital, we are never far from any child in need of a chance for treatment.<br>Together, we have treated more than 50,000 children—and today, we need your support to help equip the Burn Unit. With your support, God willing, it will begin operating very soon.<br>Every donation you make is a new step in a child’s journey to recovery.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p>في مستشفى الناس، إحنا مش بعيد عن أي طفل محتاج فرصة للعلاج.<br>إحنا مع بعض قدرنا نعالج أكثر من 50,000 طفل، والنهاردة محتاجينكم معانا علشان نجهز قسم الحروق وبيكوا ومعاكوا إن شاء الله هيشتغل في أقرب وقت.<br>كل تبرع منكم هو خطوة جديدة في رحلة الشفاء.</p>\"}', NULL, '{\"en\":\"al nas hospital\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\" Al Nas Hospital Clinical Programs\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"al nas hospital\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"Departments\",\"ar\":null}', '{\"en\":\"<p>The Clinical Nutrition Department provides nutrition support to all hospital inpatients including total parenteral &amp; enteral nutrition. In addition to that, it integrates therapeutic diets and advanced nutritional support into the care of complex clinical cases. Our scope extends from acute inpatient management (e.g., critically ill or post-surgical patients) to chronic disease support in outpatient settings. The department also provides preventive nutrition counseling to reduce disease risk and promote long-term wellness.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '[{\"0\":{\"title\":\"out 1\",\"content\":\"<p>Our department is equipped with advanced imaging technologies including 3D echocardiography, CT, and MRI, ensuring precise diagnostics, safer interventions, and improved outcomes.<\\/p><p>With renowned professors and consultants who bring international expertise, we excel in treating complex and high-risk cases such as chronic total occlusions, high-risk percutaneous interventions, and adult congenital heart disease.<\\/p><p>Care is delivered through a collaborative heart team approach that integrates cardiologists, surgeons, and imaging specialists, supported by extensive case experience, innovative non-surgical options such as TAVI and TAVR, and a strong commitment to minimally invasive procedures for faster recovery.<\\/p><p>As a teaching hospital, we are dedicated to academic excellence through fellowships, international collaborations, and continuous training.<\\/p><p>Our patient-centered model ensures accessible, lifelong care including specialized adult congenital programs, while maintaining the highest standards of quality, safety, and evidence-based practice through ongoing audits and performance reviews.<\\/p>\",\"embed\":null},\"1\":{\"title\":\"out 2\",\"content\":\"<p>Our department is equipped with advanced imaging technologies including 3D echocardiography, CT, and MRI, ensuring precise diagnostics, safer interventions, and improved outcomes.<\\/p><p>With renowned professors and consultants who bring international expertise, we excel in treating complex and high-risk cases such as chronic total occlusions, high-risk percutaneous interventions, and adult congenital heart disease.<\\/p><p>Care is delivered through a collaborative heart team approach that integrates cardiologists, surgeons, and imaging specialists, supported by extensive case experience, innovative non-surgical options such as TAVI and TAVR, and a strong commitment to minimally invasive procedures for faster recovery.<\\/p><p>As a teaching hospital, we are dedicated to academic excellence through fellowships, international collaborations, and continuous training.<\\/p><p>Our patient-centered model ensures accessible, lifelong care including specialized adult congenital programs, while maintaining the highest standards of quality, safety, and evidence-based practice through ongoing audits and performance reviews.<\\/p>\",\"embed\":null},\"content\":{\"en\":\"<p>Discover the medical specialties at Al Nas Hospital, where expert teams provide care across<\\/p>\",\"ar\":\"<p><\\/p>\"},\"embeds\":[{\"embed\":\"embed\"}],\"title\":{\"en\":\"Outcomes\",\"ar\":null}}]', '2025-12-24 08:31:48', '2026-02-11 14:32:04', NULL, 0, 0, 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=odEfPPB47XA', '{\"ar\":null}', '{\"ar\":null}', '{\"ar\":null}', '{\"ar\":null}', NULL);
INSERT INTO `department_pages` (`id`, `title`, `toptitle`, `content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1, '{\"en\":\"Medical Departments Serving Every Patient Need\",\"ar\":\"الأقسام الطبية التي تلبي جميع احتياجات المرضى\"}', '{\"en\":\"our departments \",\"ar\":\"أقسامنا\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p>Explore our centers of excellence, where multidisciplinary teams deliver advanced, specialized care across a wide range of medical fields.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p>اكتشف التخصصات الطبية في مستشفى الناس، حيث تقدم فرقنا المتخصصة رعاية متكاملة في مختلف المجالات الطبية.</p>\"}', NULL, '2026-02-12 13:53:37');
INSERT INTO `department_programs` (`id`, `title`, `department_id`, `department_speciality_id`, `description`, `why`, `success_rate`, `cases_no`, `years_no`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `order_column`) VALUES
(1, '{\"ar\":\"قسم 1\",\"en\":\"TAVI program\"}', 2, 19, '{\"en\":\"<p>Transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI) is a minimally invasive method of replacing your heart&#039;s aortic valve without open heart surgery. It was originally developed as an alternative to surgery for patients who are too sick to undergo surgery, but now, it is being used more widely for less sick patients as well.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p>22</p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p><strong>Transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI) is a minimally invasive method of replacing your heart&#039;s aortic valve without open heart surgery. It was originally developed as an alternative to surgery for patients who are too sick to undergo surgery, but now, it is being used more widely for less sick patients as well.</strong></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p>44</p>\"}', '97', '32', '3', '2025-12-25 06:30:08', '2026-01-27 13:13:28', NULL),
(3, '{\"en\":\"CTO Program\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 19, '{\"en\":\"<p>CTO is an abbreviation for chronic total occlusion of the coronary arteries, which means that one or more of the arteries that supply your heart got totally obstructed and this obstruction happened a long time ago (more than 6 months). This also means that trying to fix this issue would be problematic and complex, necessitating special instruments and a certain level of experience.<br>Not every CTO needs fixing. First, we do some investigations to make sure that you will benefit from this complex procedure –if so, we will go on with the procedure. We have enough experience to do it with the least possible risk. We have done 150 cases in the past 2 years with 88% success rate (which is comparable to the international rate).</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '88', '150', '2', '2026-01-04 17:03:20', '2026-01-27 16:16:04', NULL),
(4, '{\"en\":\"Acute Burn Management\",\"ar\":null}', 7, 26, '{\"en\":\"<p>Immediate emergency care for patients with thermal, chemical, and electrical burns, focusing on resuscitation, wound stabilization, and infection prevention.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-21 16:16:53', '2026-01-21 16:16:53', NULL),
(5, '{\"en\":\"Burn Intensive Care\",\"ar\":null}', 7, 26, '{\"en\":\"<p>Specialized critical care for patients with major burns, including advanced monitoring, ventilatory support, fluid management, and multidisciplinary intensive care</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-21 16:17:34', '2026-01-21 16:17:34', NULL),
(6, '{\"en\":\"Surgical Burn Care\",\"ar\":null}', 7, 26, '{\"en\":\"<p>Comprehensive surgical management including debridement, skin grafting, and wound closure techniques to promote recovery and reduce complications.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-21 16:18:23', '2026-01-21 16:18:23', NULL),
(7, '{\"en\":\"Burn Rehabilitation\",\"ar\":null}', 7, 26, '{\"en\":\"<p>Long-term care focusing on physical therapy, mobility restoration, scar management, and psychological support to optimize quality of life after recovery</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-21 16:22:54', '2026-01-21 16:27:35', NULL),
(8, '{\"en\":\"Pediatric Burn Care\",\"ar\":null}', 7, 26, '{\"en\":\"<p>Tailored burn management for children, addressing their unique physiological and psychological needs with family-centered support</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-21 16:23:47', '2026-01-21 16:23:47', NULL),
(9, '{\"en\":\"Infection Control & Wound Care\",\"ar\":null}', 7, 26, '{\"en\":\"<p>Specialized dressing techniques, negative pressure wound therapy, and infection prevention protocols for optimal healing.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-21 16:24:20', '2026-01-21 16:24:20', NULL),
(10, '{\"en\":\"Pain Management & Supportive Care\",\"ar\":null}', 7, 26, '{\"en\":\"<p>Multimodal pain relief, sedation, and psychological support for patients and families to improve comfort during treatment and recovery.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-21 16:25:13', '2026-01-21 16:27:22', NULL),
(11, '{\"en\":\"Outpatient Burn Follow-Up\",\"ar\":null}', 7, 26, '{\"en\":\"<p>Ongoing outpatient clinics for monitoring wound healing, functional recovery, and long-term scar assessment.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-21 16:26:04', '2026-01-21 16:26:04', NULL),
(12, '{\"en\":\"Assessments and Diagnosis\",\"ar\":null}', 10, 30, '{\"en\":\"<p>Our psychiatry department provides thorough clinical assessments for both inpatients and outpatients, integrating psychiatric history, mental status examinations, and standardized diagnostic scales. These evaluations enable precise identification of psychiatric disorders, comorbid medical conditions, and psychosocial stressors, for individualized treatment planning and multidisciplinary care</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-22 16:05:44', '2026-01-22 16:05:44', NULL),
(13, '{\"en\":\"Pharmacotherapy\",\"ar\":null}', 10, 30, '{\"en\":\"<p>We offer evidence-based pharmacological treatment tailored to each patient’s diagnosis, clinical presentation, and comorbidities, using the latest psychotropic agents—including antidepressants, antipsychotics, mood stabilizers, and anxiolytics—while closely monitoring therapeutic response, side-effect profiles, and drug interactions, ensuring safe and effective management of both acute and chronic psychiatric conditions.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-22 16:06:41', '2026-01-22 16:06:41', NULL),
(14, '{\"en\":\"Supportive Psychotherapy\",\"ar\":null}', 10, 30, '{\"en\":\"<p>Supportive psychotherapy is provided as an integral component of patient care, aimed at enhancing resilience and improving psychological functioning. This modality emphasizes strengthening coping mechanisms, reducing distress, and reinforcing adaptive behaviors, particularly for patients experiencing adjustment disorders, chronic medical illnesses, or stress-related conditions.</p><p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-22 16:07:36', '2026-01-22 16:07:36', NULL),
(15, '{\"en\":\"Behavioral Modification\",\"ar\":null}', 10, 30, '{\"en\":\"<p>Behavioral modification programs employ structured, evidence-based strategies such as reinforcement, modeling, and habit-reversal training. These approaches are particularly effective in managing maladaptive behaviors affecting mental health and general medical condition, improving adherence to treatment, and reducing risk behaviors, with strong applications in conditions such as substance use disorders, obsessive-compulsive spectrum disorders, and impulse control disorders.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-22 16:08:22', '2026-01-22 16:08:22', NULL),
(16, '{\"en\":\"Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT)\",\"ar\":null}', 10, 30, '{\"en\":\"<p>CBT is a cornerstone of our clinical services, targeting maladaptive cognitive patterns that contribute to psychiatric symptoms. By combining cognitive restructuring with behavioral interventions, CBT effectively addresses depression, anxiety disorders, post-traumatic stress disorder, and obsessive-compulsive disorder, among others. Treatment is individualized, goal-oriented, and focused on achieving sustainable, long-term improvements in psychological health.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-22 16:09:08', '2026-01-22 16:09:08', NULL),
(17, '{\"en\":\"Dialectical Behavioral Therapy (DBT)\",\"ar\":null}', 10, 30, '{\"en\":\"<p>DBT is offered as a specialized intervention for patients with severe emotional dysregulation, self-harming behaviors, and borderline personality disorder. This structured therapy integrates cognitive-behavioral techniques with mindfulness-based strategies, emphasizing emotion regulation, distress tolerance, interpersonal effectiveness, and self-acceptance. DBT is delivered in both individual and group settings to maximize outcomes and support patient recovery.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-22 16:13:17', '2026-01-22 16:13:17', NULL),
(18, '{\"en\":\"Outpatient Nutrition Services\",\"ar\":null}', 27, 24, '{\"en\":\"<p>Our outpatient nutrition services provide tailored dietary counseling and disease-specific interventions for patients across all major hospital specialties, including cardiovascular, burn, gastrointestinal, diabetes, and liver transplant care. Every patient receives an individualized nutrition plan adapted to their medical condition, lifestyle, and cultural preferences. Structured education sessions empower patients to adopt sustainable lifestyle changes, improve disease management, and enhance long-term health outcomes.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-22 16:29:39', '2026-01-22 16:29:39', NULL),
(19, '{\"en\":\" Inpatient Nutrition Services\",\"ar\":null}', 27, 24, '{\"en\":\"<p>The inpatient nutrition program ensures that hospitalized patients benefit from comprehensive nutritional support as part of their treatment plan. Whether in cardiovascular, surgical, burn, or transplant care, our team works closely with physicians, nurses, and specialists to provide the right nutrition strategy. Services range from bedside counseling to advanced enteral and parenteral feeding, all designed to accelerate recovery, promote wound healing, and reduce complications.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-22 16:30:20', '2026-01-22 16:30:20', NULL),
(20, '{\"en\":\"Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN)\",\"ar\":null}', 27, 24, '{\"en\":\"<p>The TPN program delivers life-sustaining intravenous nutrition for patients who cannot be fed orally or enterally. Customized formulations are prepared based on each patient’s medical condition and metabolic needs, serving critical care, surgical, transplant, and gastrointestinal patients. With strict safety measures, expert monitoring, and evidence-based protocols, the program ensures optimal nutritional balance, supporting recovery and reducing treatment-related risks.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-22 16:31:01', '2026-01-22 16:31:01', NULL),
(21, '{\"en\":\"Kitchen as an Outlet for Healthy Meals\",\"ar\":null}', 27, 24, '{\"en\":\"<p>Our hospital kitchen operates as a health-promoting hub, offering meals that align with medical and nutritional standards. Designed under the supervision of the Clinical Nutrition Department, menus are customized to meet the diverse needs of patients across all specialties including cardiac-friendly diets, high-protein burn recovery meals, obesity and underweight management plans, as well as renal, hepatic, and cancer-specific nutrition. By prioritizing fresh, balanced, and safe food, this program enhances recovery, strengthens outcomes, and extends wellness to staff and visitors.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-22 16:31:30', '2026-01-22 16:31:30', NULL),
(22, '{\"en\":\"Kitchen as an Outlet for Gluten Sensitivity\",\"ar\":null}', 27, 24, '{\"en\":\"<p>To support patients with celiac disease or gluten sensitivity, the hospital kitchen provides certified gluten-free meals prepared under strict safety and contamination-control protocols. This service ensures that patients in all departments, particularly those in long-term care such as gastrointestinal and transplant units, receive safe, nutritious, and enjoyable meals. By integrating gluten-free options into hospital nutrition, we help patients manage their condition confidently during their hospital stay.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-22 16:32:04', '2026-01-22 16:32:04', NULL),
(23, '{\"en\":\"Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM) \",\"ar\":null}', 6, 22, '{\"en\":\"<p>The CGM Program provides patients with real-time glucose monitoring for better management of blood sugar fluctuations. Using sensors that record glucose levels continuously, patients and physicians gain valuable insights into patterns, enabling more precise treatment adjustments.</p><ul><li><p>Professional CGM (short-term diagnostic use).</p></li><li><p>Personal CGM (long-term wearable use).</p></li><li><p>Trend analysis and data integration with clinical visits.</p></li><li><p>Training for patients and caregivers on sensor use and data interpretation.</p></li></ul>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '100', '45', '1', '2026-01-22 16:37:19', '2026-02-15 17:49:35', NULL),
(24, '{\"en\":\" Insulin Pump Therapy \",\"ar\":null}', 6, 22, '{\"en\":\"<p>The Insulin Pump Program offers advanced insulin delivery systems that mimic physiological insulin release. Pumps provide both basal and bolus insulin with programmable flexibility, helping patients achieve optimal glycemic control.</p><ul><li><p>Assessment and patient selection for pump therapy.</p></li><li><p>Pump initiation and insulin dose titration.</p></li><li><p>24/7 technical and medical support.</p></li><li><p>Follow-up visits for download, data review, and fine-tuning.</p></li><li><p>Integration with CGM for hybrid closed-loop systems.</p></li></ul>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '100', '30', '1', '2026-01-22 16:38:14', '2026-02-15 17:50:09', NULL),
(25, '{\"en\":\"Ozaki operation\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 19, '{\"en\":\"<p>The Ozaki procedure is a relatively new procedure which was first carried out in Japan.</p><p>It involves creating new valve segments (leaflets) from either your own pericardium (the covering of the heart) or bovine pericardium (the covering surrounding a cow&#039;s heart)</p><p>Specialist equipment is used to measure the diseased part of the valve. These measurements are used to cut replacement tissue to the exact size. The strips of tissue are sewn precisely into place which allows the valve to function in its normal way.</p><p>There are a number of benefits to this procedure when compared to valve replacement including:</p><p>∙  No need to take lifelong anticoagulant drug therapy which can have side effects and lifestyle limitations when taken long term</p><p>∙  Evidence from Japan shows that this type of repair typically lasts longer than replacing the valve completely (particularly for patients under 60 years of age). Most biological implants made from animal tissue need to be replaced after 8 to 15 years. <br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '98', '105', NULL, '2026-01-22 16:44:22', '2026-01-27 19:36:04', NULL),
(26, '{\"en\":\"Mitral valve repair\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 19, '{\"en\":\"<p>The mitral valve is the one situated between the left atrium and left ventricle. When damaged, the usual action is to replace it with a mechanical valve. But the better approach is to repair the damage valve without replacing it in certain situations. The advantage is to preserve the natural valve, which is better on the long term, and to avoid using anticoagulant drugs, which are very troublesome to manage. The repair procedure is a technically demanding and needs extensive experience and training. We are proud to offer this procedure with all its varieties to our patients.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '97.5', '120', NULL, '2026-01-22 16:45:21', '2026-01-27 19:36:16', NULL),
(27, '{\"en\":\"Valve-sparing aortic root replacement\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 19, '{\"en\":\"<p>Some patients have significant dilatation of the aortic root that is at risk of rupture. In our hospital, we treat those conditions by a special operation called valve-sparing aortic root replacement, which has several variations (including Tyron-David and Yacoub procedures).</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '98', '75', NULL, '2026-01-22 16:46:23', '2026-01-27 19:36:29', NULL),
(28, '{\"en\":\"HOCM septal myectomy\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 19, '{\"en\":\"<p>HOCM is a serious genetic condition that is inherited from the parents. It can cause sudden death in severe cases. Septal myectomy is a very successful operation that reduces the chances of sudden death and relieves any symptoms that can be related to this condition. We also offer the patient genetic counseling and screening for the whole family.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', ' 98', ' 55', NULL, '2026-01-22 16:49:59', '2026-01-27 19:36:57', NULL),
(29, '{\"en\":\"Minimally invasive aortic surgery\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 19, '{\"en\":\"<p>We have successfully started a special program for replacing the severely calcified and stenosed aortic valve through a very small incision, and avoid opening the chest. This enhances rapid recovery, hospital discharge and early return to the normal daily activities.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '99', ' 45', NULL, '2026-01-22 16:51:13', '2026-01-27 19:37:09', NULL),
(30, '{\"en\":\"Minimally invasive coronary surgery (MIDCAB)\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 19, '{\"en\":\"<p>We have successfully started a special program for bypass surgery through a very small incision that avoids opening up the whole chest bone. This enhances rapid recovery, hospital discharge and early return to the normal daily activities.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '98', '40', NULL, '2026-01-22 16:52:21', '2026-01-27 19:37:21', NULL),
(31, '{\"en\":\"Minimally invasive mitral valve surgery\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 19, '{\"en\":\"<p>We are about to start this program which repairs the damaged mitral valve through a very small incision that avoids opening up the whole chest bone. This enhances rapid recovery, hospital discharge and early return to the normal daily activities.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', ' 100', '18', NULL, '2026-01-22 16:53:10', '2026-01-27 19:37:34', NULL),
(32, '{\"en\":\"Unifocalization of the pulmonary arteries\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 21, '{\"en\":\"<p>Pulmonary atresia with ventricular septal defect and major aortopulmonary collateral arteries (PA/VSD/MAPCAs) is complex and heterogeneous condition. Our approach to this lesion emphasizes early complete repair with the incorporation of all lung segments and extensive lobar and segmental pulmonary artery reconstruction.</p><p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '85', '18', NULL, '2026-01-22 16:56:14', '2026-01-27 19:37:46', NULL),
(33, '{\"en\":\"Cone repair of tricuspid valve in Ebstein’s anomaly\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 21, '{\"en\":\"<p>Tricuspid valve repair using tissues from the heart and it’s rare congenital anomaly that leads to many problems and complete damage that worsen if not treated.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '98', '18', NULL, '2026-01-22 16:57:43', '2026-01-27 19:37:59', NULL),
(34, '{\"en\":\"Nikaido operation\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 21, '{\"en\":\"<p>Patients with transposition of great arteries who cannot be repaired by arterial switch operation in early life. Another way of repair can be offered which include translocation of aortic valve with both coronaries from the right ventricle to the left ventricle.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '50', '4', NULL, '2026-01-22 16:58:35', '2026-01-27 19:38:12', NULL),
(35, '{\"en\":\"TOF repair\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 21, '{\"en\":\"<p>Tetralogy of Fallot is made up of the following four defects of the heart and its blood vessels: A hole in the wall between the two lower chambers A narrowing of the pulmonary valve and main pulmonary artery The aortic valve, which opens to the aorta, is enlarged and seems to open from both ventricles. The muscular wall of the lower right chamber of the heart (right ventricle) is thicker than normal. Repair is usually done at the age of 4 months to repair all defects.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '97.5', '400', NULL, '2026-01-22 16:59:21', '2026-01-27 19:38:24', NULL),
(36, '{\"en\":\"Endoscopic Submucosal Dissection (ESD)\",\"ar\":null}', 9, 13, '{\"en\":\"<p>Endoscopic Submucosal Dissection (ESD) is an advanced endoscopic procedure used to remove early tumors from the digestive system without the need for major surgery. Our program is the first in Egypt fully dedicated to ESD, and we are the most experienced team nation and international wide, with more than 200 successful procedures in the last 2 years with 95% success rate (which is comparable to the international rate). This minimally invasive technique allows doctors to remove abnormal or precancerous tissue through an endoscope, helping patients recover faster, avoid large surgical wounds, and reduce hospital stays.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '95', '200', '2', '2026-01-27 16:03:43', '2026-01-27 19:35:18', NULL),
(37, '{\"en\":\"Achalasia Program for POEM\",\"ar\":null}', 9, 13, '{\"en\":\"<p>Peroral Endoscopic Myotomy (POEM) is a modern, minimally invasive endoscopic procedure used to treat achalasia, a condition where the esophagus has difficulty moving food down to the stomach. Our team is proud to run the first dedicated POEM program in Egypt, with experience that ranks among the most advanced both nationally and internationally. In just the last two years, we have successfully performed over 400 POEM procedures, achieving a 99% success rate (which is comparable to the international rate), which is fully comparable to leading international centers. This technique is performed through an endoscope without external cuts, allowing patients to enjoy faster recovery, less pain, and an improved quality of life.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '99', '400', '2', '2026-01-27 16:06:04', '2026-01-27 19:41:11', NULL),
(38, '{\"en\":\"Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD) \",\"ar\":null}', 9, 13, '{\"en\":\"<p>The Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD) Clinical Program provides specialized care for patients with Crohn’s disease and ulcerative colitis both adult and pediatrics. Our program brings together advanced diagnostic tools, expert endoscopic management, and a well-dedicated surgical team to ensure the best outcomes for patients with complex or advanced conditions. In the past two years, our team has successfully managed more than 600 patients. The program is designed to deliver care that meets international standards, focusing on improving quality of life, reducing complications, and offering comprehensive support throughout the treatment journey.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, '600', '2', '2026-01-27 16:07:33', '2026-01-27 19:43:07', NULL),
(39, '{\"en\":\"Zenker’s Diverticulum POEM (Z-POEM) \",\"ar\":null}', 9, 13, '{\"en\":\"<p>Zenker’s diverticulum is a pouch that can form in the upper esophagus, causing symptoms such as difficulty swallowing, regurgitation, and chronic cough. Z-POEM (Zenker’s Peroral Endoscopic Myotomy) is a modern, minimally invasive endoscopic procedure that safely treats this condition without the need for open surgery. Our clinical program is among the most experienced in the region, with a highly skilled team performing numerous successful cases and achieving excellent patient outcomes. In the last two years, we have successfully performed more than 50 Z-POEM procedures, with a 98% success rate comparable to international standards. This advanced approach allows for faster recovery, fewer complications, and a significant improvement in swallowing and overall quality of life.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '98', '50', '2', '2026-01-27 16:08:46', '2026-01-27 19:43:28', NULL),
(40, '{\"en\":\"Gastric POEM (G-POEM)\",\"ar\":null}', 9, 13, '{\"en\":\"<p>Gastroparesis is a condition where the stomach empties food very slowly, causing symptoms such as nausea, vomiting, bloating, and abdominal pain. G-POEM (Gastric Peroral Endoscopic Myotomy) is a minimally invasive endoscopic procedure that helps improve stomach emptying without the need for open surgery. Our team has successfully treated around 200 patients through this program, achieving a success rate of 50–80%, which is comparable to international outcomes. This advanced approach allows many patients to experience significant relief of symptoms, shorter recovery times, and better overall quality of life.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '50–80', '200', NULL, '2026-01-27 16:09:48', '2026-01-27 19:43:57', NULL),
(41, '{\"en\":\"Submucosal Tunneling Endoscopic Resection (STER)\",\"ar\":null}', 9, 13, '{\"en\":\"<p>Submucosal Tunneling Endoscopic Resection (STER) is an advanced, minimally invasive endoscopic procedure used to remove tumors that grow from the wall of the esophagus or stomach. Instead of traditional open surgery, STER is performed through an endoscope, which means no external cuts, less pain, and a quicker recovery for patients. Our program is led by a highly skilled team with extensive experience in advanced endoscopic therapies, performing numerous successful cases with excellent outcomes. In the last two years, we have successfully performed more than 150 STER procedures, achieving an 80–95% success rate, which is comparable to international standards. The goal of the STER program is to provide safe, effective, and patient-centered care, while helping patients return to normal life faster with fewer complications.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '80–95', '150', '2', '2026-01-27 16:10:48', '2026-01-27 19:44:18', NULL),
(42, '{\"en\":\"Complex Gut Motility Disorders\",\"ar\":null}', 9, 10, '{\"en\":\"<p>Our Surgical Gut Dysmotility Program addresses the most challenging cases of digestive motility disorders that have proven refractory to medical management. Our program focuses on three primary conditions:</p><ul><li><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Gastroparesis (characterized by delayed gastric emptying without mechanical obstruction)</p></li><li><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Colonic inertia (marked by the colon&#039;s failure to propel contents effectively),</p></li><li><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Chronic intestinal pseudo-obstruction (a complex disorder mimicking mechanical obstruction without any anatomical cause).</p></li></ul><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Patient care is delivered through a comprehensive multidisciplinary team approach that brings together specialized surgeons, gastroenterologists and nutritionists.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Our surgical expertise encompasses a range of advanced procedures carefully selected based on the specific motility disorder and individual patient factors. For patients with severe gastroparesis, we perform pyloroplasty to improve gastric emptying and gastric size reduction surgeries to enhance motility. Those suffering from colonic inertia may benefit from total colectomy when conservative measures have failed. For the most complex cases requiring nutritional support or decompression, we provide specialized feeding tube placements tailored to each patient&#039;s unique anatomical and physiological needs. Each surgical intervention is part of a comprehensive treatment strategy developed through our multidisciplinary collaboration, ensuring the best possible outcomes for our patients.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-27 18:42:25', '2026-01-27 19:45:56', NULL),
(43, '{\"en\":\"Intestinal Failure and Rehabilitation \",\"ar\":null}', 9, 10, '{\"en\":\"<p>Our Intestinal Rehabilitation Program is a center of excellence for adults and children living with intestinal failure, most commonly caused by Short Bowel Syndrome (SBS). We understand that it is a life-altering condition that requires highly specialized, lifelong care.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Our mission is to help patients achieve nutritional independence and significantly improve their quality of life through a comprehensive, multidisciplinary approach that combines advanced medical management, innovative surgical techniques, and continuous support.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Conditions Treated: Short Bowel Syndrome (SBS), often resulting from massive resections for Crohn&#039;s disease, ischemia, or trauma.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Our Approach: We work hand-in-hand with a dedicated Nutrition Support Team. Our surgical expertise includes bowel-lengthening procedures (like the STEP –“Serial Transverse Enteroplasty” procedure which lengthens and narrows the dilated intestine to slow transit time) to increase nutrient absorption. The ultimate goal for our patients is to wean off total parenteral nutrition (TPN) and achieve a nutritional autonomy.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-27 18:43:21', '2026-01-27 18:43:21', NULL),
(44, '{\"en\":\"Advanced Upper GI and Esophageal Surgery\",\"ar\":null}', 9, 10, '{\"en\":\"<p>Our Advanced Upper GI and Esophageal Surgery Program provides comprehensive surgical management for benign and malignant conditions affecting the esophagus and stomach. We specialize in treating a wide spectrum of diseases, including esophageal cancer, benign esophageal disorders such as end-stage motility diseases, corrosive injuries and GERD. Our program is particularly renowned for managing challenging cases, including reoperative surgery for failed prior interventions and complex reconstructive procedures.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Patient care is delivered through a dedicated multidisciplinary team (MDT) comprising esophageal surgeons, gastroenterologists, oncologists, radiologists, and nutrition specialists. This collaborative approach ensures that each treatment plan is meticulously tailored to the individual patient’s condition.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">We employ state-of-the-art minimally invasive techniques, including laparoscopic surgery, to enhance precision, reduce recovery time, and improve outcomes. Our surgical expertise includes:</p><ul><li><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Minimally invasive esophagectomy with gastric pull-up for esophageal cancer</p></li><li><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Colon bypass surgery for corrosive strictures refractory to endoscopic management</p></li><li><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Revision anti-reflux procedures for complex GERD</p></li><li><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Esophageal replacement surgeries for benign conditions such as end stage achalasia</p></li></ul><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">By combining advanced surgical techniques with a patient-centered, multidisciplinary approach, we strive to achieve the best possible oncological and functional results for every patient.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-27 18:44:17', '2026-01-27 19:45:21', NULL),
(45, '{\"en\":\"Comprehensive Surgical Oncology\",\"ar\":null}', 9, 10, '{\"en\":\"<p>Our Comprehensive Gastrointestinal Cancer Surgery Program offers advanced surgical management for malignancies affecting the entire gastrointestinal tract, with specialized expertise in upper GI, colorectal, and pancreatic cancers. We provide personalized, multimodal care for patients with esophageal, gastric, pancreatic, and colorectal malignancies, utilizing the latest surgical techniques and technology to achieve optimal oncological outcomes.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Patient management is centered around our multidisciplinary tumor board, where surgical oncologists, medical oncologists, radiation oncologists, gastroenterologists, radiologists, and pathologists collaborate to develop individualized treatment plans. This team-based approach ensures that each patient receives the most appropriate sequence of therapies.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Our surgical expertise encompasses:</p><ul><li><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Minimally invasive and conventional resections for esophageal and gastric cancers, including radical gastrectomies and esophagectomies with gastric pull-up</p></li><li><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Pancreaticoduodenectomy (Whipple procedure) and distal pancreatectomies for pancreatic cancer</p></li><li><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Advanced colorectal resections including total mesorectal excision (TME) for rectal cancer and sphincter preserving resections when feasible.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Complex multivisceral resections for locally advanced tumors requiring en-bloc removal of involved organs</p></li></ul><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">We integrate enhanced recovery after surgery (ERAS) protocols to minimize postoperative complications and accelerate recovery, ensuring our patients can promptly transition to adjuvant therapies when indicated.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-27 18:45:04', '2026-01-27 19:46:51', NULL),
(46, '{\"en\":\"Gut malrotation \",\"ar\":null}', 9, 10, '{\"en\":\"<p>Our Gut Malrotation and Complex Abdominal Surgery Program builds upon the pioneering work of Professor Aboul Magd, the founder of our department and a leading authority in the surgical management of complex abdominal disorders. We specialize in the treatment of intestinal malrotation across all age groups, from pediatric patients to adults with late-presenting cases, offering both primary corrective surgery and management of complex revisions.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Specialized Surgical Expertise: Kareem&#039;s Procedure which is a refined surgical approach developed by Professor Aboul Magd for the definitive correction of intestinal malrotation, focusing on anatomical restoration and prevention of recurrence. The program continues the legacy of Professor Aboul Magd&#039;s innovative work ensuring that patients with intestinal malrotation receive world-class surgical care rooted in decades of specialized experience and ongoing innovation</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-27 18:45:48', '2026-01-27 19:47:41', NULL),
(47, '{\"en\":\"Neonatal Surgical Training \",\"ar\":null}', 9, 11, '{\"en\":\"<p>The Neonatal Surgical Training Program is a specialized educational and clinical program designed to provide surgeons with advanced skills in managing surgical conditions in newborns. Our program focuses on the diagnosis and surgical treatment of congenital anomalies, neonatal emergencies, and critical surgical conditions that require high precision and expertise.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">This is the first program in The Egypt and the Middle East fully dedicated to structured neonatal surgical training, with a multidisciplinary approach involving neonatologists, anesthesiologists, and pediatric intensive care teams.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">The program emphasizes hands-on operative training, simulation-based skill development, and evidence-based management, ensuring that participants gain confidence in handling complex neonatal cases. By joining this program, surgeons enhance their ability to deliver safe, effective, and life-saving surgical care to newborns, ultimately improving survival rates and quality of life for the most vulnerable patients.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-27 18:52:02', '2026-01-27 18:52:02', NULL),
(48, '{\"en\":\" Basic Pediatric Laparoscopic Training\",\"ar\":null}', 9, 11, '{\"en\":\"<p>The Basic Pediatric Laparoscopic Training Program provides surgeons with the essential skills to perform minimally invasive surgery in children safely and effectively. The program is designed for pediatric surgeons seeking to acquire foundational knowledge and hands-on experience in laparoscopic techniques.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Our program includes structured training modules on instrument handling, trocar placement, ergonomics, and fundamental laparoscopic procedures such as appendectomy, hernia repair, and diagnostic laparoscopy.</p><p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\">Through simulation Dry labs, animal models, and supervised operative exposure, participants gain practical experience while adhering to international safety and competency standards. The program helps surgeons minimize operative trauma, shorten hospital stays, and enhance recovery for pediatric patients.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-27 18:52:57', '2026-01-27 18:52:57', NULL),
(49, '{\"en\":\"Prevalence and management of Celiac disease among Infants and Children with IDDM.\",\"ar\":null}', 9, 12, '{\"en\":\"<p>Celiac disease is an increasingly recognized autoimmune disorder that commonly coexists with insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus (IDDM) in children. Our program focuses on prevalence, early detection, and comprehensive management of celiac disease among infants and children living with IDDM. By combining clinical expertise with advanced diagnostic tools, we aim to identify cases at an early stage and provide individualized dietary and therapeutic interventions that improve long-term health outcomes. This initiative represents one of the first structured programs of its kind in Egypt, designed to raise awareness, standardize management protocols, and enhance the quality of life for pediatric patients facing the dual challenges of celiac disease and diabetes.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-27 18:55:01', '2026-01-27 18:55:01', NULL),
(50, '{\"en\":\"Medical Management and bowel retraining program for functional constipation in Infants and Children with IDDM.\",\"ar\":null}', 9, 12, '{\"en\":\"<p>Functional constipation is a frequent and often underestimated problem in infants and children, particularly those living with insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus (IDDM). Our program is dedicated to the medical management and bowel retraining of pediatric patients with functional constipation, with the goal of improving both gastrointestinal health and overall diabetes control. Through a structured, multidisciplinary approach, we provide individualized treatment plans that combine evidence-based pharmacologic therapy with non-pharmacologic strategies, including dietary modifications, bowel retraining, and behavioral support. This initiative aims to reduce complications, prevent recurrence, and significantly enhance the quality of life for children with IDDM who struggle with chronic constipation.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-27 18:55:58', '2026-01-27 18:55:58', NULL),
(51, '{\"en\":\"Electrophysiology\",\"ar\":null}', 2, 32, '{\"en\":\"<p>This program is designed to treat patients who have diseases related to the electric conduction system of the heart. Our hearts have a built-in conduction system consisting of fibers that connect different areas of the heart, the goal is to synchronize the contraction of all the muscles of the heart.</p><p>Diseases in the conduction system include blocks, abnormal electric tissue, and accessory pathways. In the EP lab, we can treat all these conditions efficiently with ablation techniques.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '90', '1000', '4', '2026-01-28 13:59:16', '2026-02-01 15:26:11', NULL),
(52, '{\"en\":\"Cardiac devices\",\"ar\":\" -  Copy\"}', 2, 32, '{\"en\":\"<p>Patients who develop a block in the conduction system of the heart and very slow heart rates will need pacemakers to overcome this problem.</p><p>Patients with advanced heart failure may also need a special pacemaker that improves the heart function called a CRT device.</p><p>Also, patients who have certain diseases are at risk of sudden death due to major arrhythmias. Those patients need to have an ICD device inserted, to give them internal electric shocks that abort those types of arrhythmias and prevent sudden death from happening.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-28 13:59:16', '2026-02-01 15:26:29', NULL),
(53, '{\"en\":\"Leadless Pacemaker\",\"ar\":\" -  Copy -  Copy\"}', 2, 32, '{\"en\":\"<p>A leadless pacemaker is the most innovative solution in the electrophysiology subspecialty. This new device is inserted directly into the heart without any wires or pockets in the shoulder area. This is especially important for those patients who had infections on the wires of the regular pacemakers.</p><p>We are proud to be the first hospital in Egypt who started implanting this new device.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-28 13:59:16', '2026-02-01 15:26:41', NULL),
(54, '{\"en\":\"Lead Exctraction\",\"ar\":\" -  Copy -  Copy -  Copy\"}', 2, 32, '{\"en\":\"<p>Patients who have implanted pacemaker devices may develop some problems over time (infection or lead failure) and require the complete removal of the system. However, if the devices were implanted many years ago, it would be very difficult to remove them because of the fibrosis that develops over time. This procedure is very risky and requires certain devices and expertise.</p><p>We started this program and have done several successful cases so far.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-28 13:59:16', '2026-02-01 15:26:56', NULL),
(55, '{\"en\":\"Adult Congenital Heart Interventions\",\"ar\":\" -  Copy\"}', 2, 19, '{\"en\":\"<p>What is congenital heart disease?</p><p>This means abnormalities in the structure of the heart that are due to defects in its development before birth.</p><p>Most of those defects either close on their own during childhood or require surgical or catheter-based interventions that are also done during childhood. Fortunately, this practice improved the survival and quality of life of those patients who used to not survive till adulthood in the past. Nowadays, those patients reach adulthood in good shape. However, they need continuous monitoring and management of any health issues related to the heart that emerge later in life. This management includes imaging studies (echocardiography, CT, and MRI scans), and sometimes catheter-based interventions and surgeries.</p><p>We have a specialized unit for dealing with this group of patients and their medical conditions.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '98', '220', '3', '2026-01-04 17:03:20', '2026-02-01 15:29:29', NULL),
(56, '{\"en\":\"Complex and high-risk intervention procedures (CHIP)\",\"ar\":\" -  Copy -  Copy\"}', 2, 19, '{\"en\":\"<p>Some patients have very complicated heart disease with severe calcification of the coronary arteries, borderline blood pressure, and very low cardiac contractility. These patients have an extremely high risk of complications and even death during cardiac procedures, especially if they are also very old. In order to successfully treat them, one must have the necessary dedicated equipment and clinical skills, and interventional experience. In this program, we offer those patients a chance for improvement of their medical condition to go on with their life.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '99', '100', '3', '2026-01-04 17:03:20', '2026-02-01 15:30:45', NULL),
(57, '{\"en\":\"Mitral interventions\",\"ar\":\" -  Copy -  Copy -  Copy\"}', 2, 19, '{\"en\":\"<p>The mitral valve is the one connecting the chambers of the left side of the heart and maintains blood flow in only one direction then closes to avoid its flow in the opposite direction. This valve gets destroyed in several diseases: it may become smaller in size (stenotic), thus obstructing the blood flow, or may become very large (regurgitant) and does not close properly, so that the blood flows abnormally in the opposite direction. In this program, we can treat the small valves by using special balloons that increase their size to near normal. In the pipeline, we are preparing to deal also with the regurgitant valves by using special clips.</p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p></p>\",\"ar\":\"<p></p>\"}', '100', '30', '2', '2026-01-04 17:03:20', '2026-02-01 15:32:24', NULL);
